  "title": "fix round for T-1707: test_dispatch_does_not_block asserts ordering with an Event, not a 0.5 s wall clock",
  "spec": "Evidence 2026-10-07: tests/test_daemon.py Daemon.test_dispatch_does_not_block failed the gates of T-1707 (1.24 s) and\nT-1706 (0.54 s, a task that does not touch daemon.py) while two full gates ran in parallel; it passed 3/3 alone. A wall-clock\nbound that tight turns machine load into red gates.\nFix the test, not the daemon: assert the property it guards (dispatch returns before the spawned worker finishes) with a\nsynchronisation primitive, e.g. the fake worker blocks on a threading.Event that the test sets only after dispatch returned,\nand a generous timeout (10 s) only as a hang guard. No change to orchestrator/daemon.py.\nRun: PYTHONPATH=tests uv run python -m unittest tests.test_daemon.Daemon.test_dispatch_does_not_block 20 times in a loop\nwhile another test_daemon run is in progress; all pass. Commit on the task branch.\n\nFix-round placement (Planner 2026-10-07 18:25): the test now fails 5/5 on this machine under load, on T-1707 and on the\nmerged goal/T-1667 tree alike, so every gate in this repo is red until it is fixed. Commit on task/T-1707 in wt/T-1707 (do\nnot touch T-1707's daemon.py change). The daemon re-gates wt/T-1707 with both commits.",
