        "summary": "I fixed the flaky `test_dispatch_does_not_block` without touching `orchestrator/daemon.py`, and all three acceptance checks pass.\n\nThe fake `executor.start` now waits on a `threading.Event`. The test checks that `self.started` is still empty after each of the two `tick()` calls, which proves dispatch returned before the worker finished. It then confirms the second tick did not dispatch again, sets the Event, and waits for `[a]`. The 10 s timeouts only stop a hang; nothing depends on them for timing. If an assertion fails, the Event is still set before the worker thread is joined, so the test can't hang.\n\nOne thing to check: the packet says to commit on `task/T-1707` in `wt/T-1707`, but this session started in `wt/T-1713` on `task/T-1713`. That branch already sits on T-1707's daemon commit (8620888), and I was told to commit in the current worktree, so the commit is `9dcc324` on `task/T-1713`. If the daemon re-gates `wt/T-1707`, that commit needs to be cherry-picked onto `task/T-1707` first.\n\nFiles changed:\n- `tests/test_daemon.py` (only `test_dispatch_does_not_block`)\n\nTests:\n- I ran the test 20 times in a row while a full `tests.test_daemon` run went in parallel: 20 of 20 passed.\n- The full `tests.test_daemon` run: 256 tests, OK.\n- No failures to report.",
